// #71: a segment whose timestamp is older than the last one taken is an
// old duplicate, maybe from a wrapped sequence space: it is dropped and
// answered with a duplicate ACK (PAWS, RFC 7323 §5, tcp_validate_incoming).
0      connect 192.0.2.2:80
+0     > S 0:0(0) <mss 1460,sackOK,nop,nop,TS val ? ecr 0,nop,wscale 8,eol>
+0.01  < S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win 65535 <mss 1460,sackOK,TS val 100 ecr 0,nop,wscale 7>
+0     > . 1:1(0) ack 1 <nop,nop,TS val ? ecr 100>
+0.1   < P. 1:101(100) ack 1 win 1000 <nop,nop,TS val 200 ecr 0>
+0     > . 1:1(0) ack 101 <nop,nop,TS val ? ecr 200>
+0.01  < P. 101:201(100) ack 1 win 1000 <nop,nop,TS val 150 ecr 0>
+0     > . 1:1(0) ack 101 <nop,nop,TS val ? ecr 200>
// The same data with a current timestamp is taken.
+0.01  < P. 101:201(100) ack 1 win 1000 <nop,nop,TS val 210 ecr 0>
+0     > . 1:1(0) ack 201 <nop,nop,TS val ? ecr 210>
+0     recv 200
